<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Home' }) %>
<%- include('partials/spine', { nav: 'home' }) %>

<main class="sheet">
  <span class="crop tl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop bl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop br" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="block pt-20" id="block">

    <%- include('partials/desk', { deskQuery: '' }) %>

    <%#
      ── THE MASTHEAD ──────────────────────────────────────

      A date, not a name. "You" was a title that never changed and told the
      reader nothing they did not already know; a masthead date changes
      daily, is the warmest thing on the page, and is what a paper puts in
      that position. The handle sits on the right in the folio position,
      small, where a masthead puts the edition.
    %>
    <header class="masthead">
      <h1 class="masthead-date"><%= h.fmt.longDate(today) %></h1>
      <a class="masthead-who mono-s dim no-underline" href="/@<%= user.username || user.handle %>">
        @<%= user.username || user.handle %>
      </a>
    </header>

    <%#
      WAITING ON YOU.

      A follow request is the only thing in this product that is blocked on
      an answer, so it sits above everything else and it is a panel rather
      than a line — it is the one thing on this page you are meant to act
      on. The redesign has no slot for it, because the day it was drawn
      there was nothing waiting; that is not a reason to drop the only
      control on the page.

      §3 — declining is silent. Neither button says anything about what the
      other person will be told, because they are told nothing.
    %>
    <% if (requests && requests.length) { %>
      <section class="panel front-waiting">
        <h2 class="sec">Waiting on you</h2>
        <% requests.forEach(function(r) { %>
          <div class="pigeon-row">
            <%- h.avatarPlate(r, { size: 30, className: 'pigeon-face' }) %>
            <span class="pigeon-main">
              <a class="no-underline" href="/@<%= r.username %>"><%= r.display_name || '@' + r.username %></a>
              <span class="dim">asked to follow you</span>
            </span>
            <span class="pigeon-acts">
              <form method="post" action="/settings/requests/<%= r.follower_id %>/approve" class="inline-form">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="home">
                <button class="more-link mono-s" type="submit">LET THEM IN</button>
              </form>
              <form method="post" action="/settings/requests/<%= r.follower_id %>/decline" class="inline-form">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <input type="hidden" name="from" value="home">
                <button class="more-link mono-s dim" type="submit">NO</button>
              </form>
            </span>
          </div>
        <% }) %>
      </section>
    <% } %>

    <%#
      ABOUT YOU — the pigeonhole, folded in. §10 still governs: no counts in
      the navigation, no "mark all as read". Reading them is what clears
      them, which is a side effect of opening this page.
    %>
    <% if (notices && notices.length) { %>
      <section class="panel front-notices">
        <h2 class="sec">About you</h2>
        <% notices.forEach(function(g) { %>
          <div class="pigeon-row<%= g.unread ? ' is-unread' : '' %>">
            <span class="pigeon-main">
              <%= h.actorLine(g.actors) %> <span class="dim"><%= g.subject %></span>
            </span>
            <span class="pigeon-acts">
              <% if (g.url) { %><a class="more-link mono-s" href="<%= g.url %>">OPEN →</a><% } %>
            </span>
          </div>
        <% }) %>
      </section>
    <% } %>

    <%#
      ── THE FRONT ─────────────────────────────────────────

      Three bands, and each answers a different question.

        on press      what am I inside of        — jackets, at a size
        where you are where does the rest stand  — season, pile, clubs
        latest        what has everyone done     — the feed, two up

      The rail is gone. It had become a column of six unrelated things
      stacked in a 260px gutter — a lead jacket, two books, a season, and
      whatever else arrived — read top to bottom in a strip narrower than
      the covers it was showing. The books are the object this product is
      about, so they get the width.
    %>

    <%#
      WHAT IS ON PRESS.

      Three jackets at plate size, the page number burned into the foot of
      each. The front page used to carry one lead jacket and then describe
      the other two in type; showing all three as objects is both simpler
      and more use, because which book you pick up is a decision made by
      looking at them.
    %>
    <div class="front-duo">

      <section class="front-col">
        <h2 class="front-h2">
          <span>On press</span>
          <% if (reading.length) { %>
            <a class="more-link mono-s" href="/reading">ALL <%= reading.length %> →</a>
          <% } %>
        </h2>

        <% if (!reading.length) { %>
          <p class="note front-empty">
            Nothing on press. <a class="more-link mono-s" href="/desk">FIND A BOOK →</a>
          </p>
        <% } else { %>
          <div class="press-shelf">
            <% reading.slice(0, 3).forEach(function(b) { %>
              <a class="shelf-bk" href="/work/<%= b.work_id %>">
                <span class="shelf-jk">
                  <%- h.frame({ cover_url: b.cover_url, cover_cache_key: b.cover_cache_key,
                                title: b.title, authorLine: b.authorLine,
                                trimAspect: b.trimAspect, isbn13: b.isbn13,
                                work_id: b.work_id }) %>
                  <%# The page, on the jacket. It is the one number on this
                      page anybody acts on, and it belongs on the object it
                      describes rather than in a column beside it. %>
                  <span class="shelf-page">
                    <b><%= b.current_page ? h.fmt.position(b.current_page, b.position_type) : '—' %></b>
                    <span class="mono-s"><%= b.totalPositions ? 'OF ' + b.totalPositions
                                                              : h.positionLabel(b.position_type) %></span>
                  </span>
                </span>

                <%# A filled bar here, not the reading page's mark.
                    "A fill is a score and a mark is just where you are" was
                    written for a press row, which is tall enough for a 9px
                    tick to read as a position on a rule. Under a jacket the
                    rule is a 2px base line and the tick straddled the
                    jacket's own edge, reading as a stray orange fleck rather
                    than as progress. At this size the fill IS the position.
                    A book with no extent gets a broken rule, because there
                    is no line to be somewhere along yet. %>
                <span class="shelf-prog<%= b.totalPositions ? '' : ' is-unknown' %>"<%
                      if (b.percent) { %> role="img" aria-label="<%= b.percent %> percent"<% } %>>
                  <% if (b.percent) { %>
                    <i id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'hp', b.work_id, 'width:' + h.css.pct(b.percent)) %>"></i>
                  <% } %>
                </span>

                <span class="shelf-t"><%= h.shortTitle(b.title, { max: 46 }) %></span>
                <span class="shelf-by mono-s"><%= b.authorLine %></span>
                <% if (b.daysSinceLog != null) { %>
                  <span class="shelf-gap mono-s<%= b.stalled ? ' is-stale' : '' %>">
                    <%= h.sinceLabel(b.daysSinceLog).replace('LAST LOGGED ', '') %>
                  </span>
                <% } else if (b.started_at) { %>
                  <span class="shelf-gap mono-s">STARTED TODAY</span>
                <% } %>
              </a>
            <% }) %>
          </div>
        <% } %>
      </section>

      <%#
        WHERE YOU ARE.

        Three standings, none of them a metric: the season you are in, the
        pile you are not reading, and the clubs waiting on you. The pile is
        the largest single fact about this library and the front page said
        nothing about it at all.
      %>
      <section class="front-col">
        <h2 class="front-h2"><span>Where you are</span></h2>

        <% if (season) { %>
          <div class="where-card">
            <div class="where-k mono-s">
              <span>SEASON <%= season.short %></span>
              <% if (season.state === 'open') { %><em class="is-open">OPEN</em><% } %>
            </div>
            <% if (season.strip.length) { %>
              <a class="where-strip no-underline" href="/season/<%= season.code %>"
                 role="img" aria-label="<%= h.stripLabel(season.strip) %>">
                <% season.strip.forEach(function(b) { %>
                  <i class="<%= h.bandClass(b) %>"<% if (b.hex) { %> id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'hs', b.hex, 'background:' + h.css.color(b.hex)) %>"<% } %>></i>
                <% }) %>
              </a>
            <% } %>
            <a class="where-sub mono-s no-underline" href="/season/<%= season.code %>">
              <%= season.count ? season.count + ' SO FAR' : 'NOTHING YET' %>
            </a>
          </div>
        <% } %>

        <%#
          NEXT FROM THE PILE.

          The pile card used to be a count and a row of spines — the largest
          fact about the library, stated and left there. It now carries three
          books to actually read, which is the difference between a pile that
          accuses you and one that is useful.

          The count survives as the card's own badge, so nothing is lost.

          Every line under a title is derived: which finished books this one
          sits nearest, or how long it has been held. No sentence here is
          written by a model, and the card never says it learned anything —
          it is similarity ranking over content, and §01 of the spec is
          explicit that the word "learning" must not attach to it.
        %>
        <% if (recos && recos.length) { %>
          <div class="where-card">
            <div class="where-k mono-s">
              <span>NEXT FROM THE PILE</span>
              <% if (waiting) { %><em class="is-quiet"><%= waiting.count %> UNREAD</em><% } %>
            </div>
            <div class="pile-recos">
              <% recos.forEach(function(r) { %>
                <a class="pile-reco" href="/work/<%= r.work_id %>">
                  <span class="pile-cv">
                    <%- h.frame({ cover_url: r.cover_url, cover_cache_key: r.cover_cache_key,
                                  title: r.title, work_id: r.work_id }) %>
                  </span>
                  <span class="pile-m">
                    <span class="pile-n"><%= h.shortTitle(r.title, { max: 30 }) %></span>
                    <span class="pile-a mono-s">
                      <%= (r.author || 'Unknown').toUpperCase() %><%
                        if (r.heldDays) { %> · HELD <%= r.heldDays.toLocaleString() %> DAYS<% } %>
                    </span>
                    <% if (r.neighbourTitles.length) { %>
                      <span class="pile-why">Nearest to <%
                        r.neighbourTitles.forEach(function(t, i) { %><%
                          if (i) { %> and <% } %><b><%= h.shortTitle(t, { max: 26 }) %></b><%
                        }) %></span>
                    <% } %>
                  </span>
                </a>
              <% }) %>
            </div>
            <span class="where-sub mono-s">RANKED ON WIKIPEDIA PLOT SUMMARIES</span>
          </div>
        <% } else if (waiting) { %>
          <div class="where-card">
            <div class="where-k mono-s"><span>WAITING</span></div>
            <a class="where-big no-underline" href="/shelf/waiting">
              <span class="where-v"><%= waiting.count %></span>
              <span class="where-u">unopened</span>
            </a>
            <%# Only the editions with a sampled spine are drawn. A made-up
                colour on a shelf of real ones is a lie about which books
                are which. %>
            <% if (waiting.spines.length) { %>
              <span class="where-spines" aria-hidden="true">
                <% waiting.spines.forEach(function(c) { %>
                  <i id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'sp', c, 'background:' + h.css.color(c)) %>"></i>
                <% }) %>
              </span>
            <% } %>
            <% if (waiting.heldDays) { %>
              <span class="where-sub mono-s">OLDEST HELD <%= waiting.heldDays.toLocaleString() %> DAYS</span>
            <% } %>
          </div>
        <% } %>

        <% if (clubs && clubs.length) { %>
          <div class="where-card">
            <div class="where-k mono-s">
              <span>CLUBS</span>
              <em class="is-in"><%= clubs.length %> IN</em>
            </div>
            <% clubs.forEach(function(c) { %>
              <a class="where-club no-underline" href="/clubs/<%= c.slug %>">
                <span class="where-em">
                  <% if (c.avatar_key) { %>
                    <img src="/avatar/<%= c.avatar_key %>/128" alt="" width="38" height="38">
                  <% } else { %>
                    <span class="grp-emblem-blank" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <% } %>
                </span>
                <span>
                  <span class="where-n"><%= h.shortTitle(c.name, { max: 26 }) %></span>
                  <span class="where-d mono-s">
                    <%= c.on_display ? h.shortTitle(c.on_display, { max: 28 }) : 'NOTHING ON DISPLAY' %>
                    · <%= c.members %> IN
                  </span>
                </span>
              </a>
            <% }) %>
          </div>
        <% } %>
      </section>
    </div>

    <%#
      LATEST, two up.

      The thumbnail varies with what happened, because the events are not
      all about the same kind of thing: a finished book shows its jacket, a
      closed season shows its strip, a club shows its emblem. Where there is
      no object — or no jacket held — the reader's own face stands in, which
      is the edge this feed carried on every row before.

      A jacket at 20px was an unreadable smudge and that argument stood; at
      38px on a 2:3 trim it is a legible thumbnail, which is a different
      thing. The season strip is the one place a derived colour appears
      here, and it appears as the season's own strip rather than as a tint
      on somebody else's row.
    %>
    <section class="front-latest">
      <h2 class="front-h2">
        <span>Latest</span>
        <% if (feed.length) { %><a class="more-link mono-s" href="/wall">ALL ACTIVITY →</a><% } %>
      </h2>

      <% if (!feed.length) { %>
        <p class="note front-empty">Nothing this week. This fills up when you follow people.</p>
      <% } else { %>
        <div class="front-evs">
          <% feed.forEach(function(e) { %>
            <%
              var href = e.kind === 'season' ? '/@' + e.username + '/' + e.code
                       : (e.kind === 'club' || e.kind === 'announcement') ? '/clubs/' + e.slug
                       : '/work/' + e.work_id;
              var verb = { finished: 'finished', review: 'reviewed', season: 'closed',
                           club: 'joined', announcement: 'announced' }[e.kind] || 'logged';
            %>
            <a class="front-ev" href="<%= href %>">
              <span class="ev-mini">
                <% if (e.kind === 'season' && e.strip && e.strip.length) { %>
                  <span class="ev-strip" aria-hidden="true">
                    <% e.strip.forEach(function(b) { %>
                      <i<% if (b.hex) { %> id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'hs', b.hex, 'background:' + h.css.color(b.hex)) %>"<% } %>></i>
                    <% }) %>
                  </span>
                <% } else if (e.cover_url || e.cover_cache_key) { %>
                  <%- h.frame({ cover_url: e.cover_url, cover_cache_key: e.cover_cache_key,
                                title: e.title, work_id: e.work_id }) %>
                <% } else { %>
                  <%- h.avatarPlate(e, { size: 38, className: 'ev-face' }) %>
                <% } %>
              </span>

              <span class="ev-txt">
                <b>@<%= e.username %></b> <%= verb %>
                <i><%= e.title || e.club_name %></i><%
                  if (e.kind === 'finished' && e.items && e.items.length > 1) { %>
                  and <%= e.items.length - 1 %> more<% }
                  if (e.stars != null) { %> · <%= h.starText(e.stars) %><% } %>
                <% if (e.caption) { %><span class="ev-cap"><%= e.caption %></span><% } %>
              </span>

              <span class="ev-when mono-s"><%= e.ago %></span>
            </a>
          <% }) %>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-end note">That\u2019s everything from this week.</p>
      <% } %>
    </section>
  </div>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
